  "question": "For $$f(x)=(2x^2+3x-1)^5,$$ find $f'(x)$ and hence calculate $f'(1)$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "<b>Differentiating the composite function</b><br>Let $u=2x^2+3x-1$. Then $f(x)=u^5$.<br>$$\\frac{df}{du}=5u^4,\\qquad \\frac{du}{dx}=4x+3$$<br>Hence, $$f'(x)=5(2x^2+3x-1)^4(4x+3)$$<br><b>Evaluation at $x=1$</b><br>At $x=1$, $$2x^2+3x-1=4\\quad\\text{and}\\quad 4x+3=7$$<br>Therefore, $$f'(1)=5(4)^4(7)=5\\times256\\times7=8960$$",
